member.summary:
Nulls are omitted everywhere. A value-type property is omitted when it equals the type's default only if the
class initializer leaves it at that default too (so "ShowGridLines = true" or "Zoom = 100" are always written;
omitting a false/0 there would silently change meaning on reload).

Registers a named data provider usable by templates (data set Type "provider"): your code returns the data
(EF query, Dapper, DataTable, JSON, any list) from the report parameters.
o.AddProvider("Orders", p => db.Orders.Where(x => x.Year == (int)p["Year"]).ToList());

A small report server: /reports lists the reports you registered with options.AddReport(...);
/reports/{name} shows one with a parameter form and download buttons; ?format=pdf|xlsx|docx|csv|html|png returns a file.
Host-neutral (ASP.NET Core and System.Web adapters call ). Authorization is the host's job.
